note('Author page 8; archive pencil number 26. Formulas (20)–(25 bis) parameterise u by gamma (or p) and eta, then introduce beta, alpha, and tilde-alpha. The diagonal NB has u\u2032=tau(u), eta\u2032=tau_infinity(eta), a separate beta clause, and a separate lambda clause. H conflates the last two. In the replacement definition at (24), the ink has l_1^gamma; the cancelled draft to its left has l_1^(-gamma). The positive replacement is retained irrespective of the identities one might expect. The relation beta sigma_infinity(beta)=1 follows formally from (23) provided sigma_infinity is involutive; this conditional cancellation was checked, not the full groupoid argument. The manuscript omits soit in its first NB and est before conséquence, and those omissions are preserved.')
